## Overview

This document outlines the best practices, conventions, and standards used in the LTI frontend application. These practices ensure code consistency, maintainability, and optimal development experience.

## Technology Stack

### Core Technologies
- **React 18.3.1**: Modern React with functional components and hooks
- **TypeScript 5.9.3**: For type safety and better development experience
- **Vite 5.2.0**: Build tooling and development server (replaces Create React App)
- **React Router DOM 6.28.2**: Client-side routing and navigation

### UI Framework
- **Chakra UI 3.29.0**: Component library for React (v3 API)
- **@chakra-ui/color-mode 2.2.0**: Color mode management for Chakra UI
- **@emotion/react 11.14.0**: CSS-in-JS library (required by Chakra UI)
- **@emotion/styled 11.14.1**: Styled components for Emotion
- **framer-motion 12.23.24**: Animation library (used by Chakra UI)
- **react-icons 5.5.0**: Icon library (replaces React Bootstrap Icons)

### State Management & Data Flow
- **React Hooks**: useState, useEffect for local component state
- **TanStack Query 5.90.9**: Server state management and data fetching
- **Zustand 5.0.8**: Lightweight client state management
- **Axios 1.13.2**: HTTP client for API communication

### Form Handling & Validation
- **React Hook Form 7.66.0**: Form state management
- **Zod 4.1.12**: Schema validation library
- **@hookform/resolvers 5.2.2**: Zod resolver for React Hook Form

### Testing Framework
- **Vitest 4.0.9**: Unit and integration testing (replaces Jest)
- **React Testing Library 16.3.0**: Component testing utilities
- **@testing-library/jest-dom 6.9.1**: Custom Jest matchers for DOM
- **@testing-library/user-event 14.6.1**: User interaction simulation
- **Storybook 10.0.7**: Component development and documentation

### Development Tools
- **ESLint 9.39.1**: Code linting with React-specific rules
- **TypeScript**: Static type checking with strict mode
- **Vite**: Fast build tool with HMR (Hot Module Replacement)

