### Form Handling with React Hook Form + Zod
- Use **React Hook Form** for form state management
- Use **Zod** for schema validation
- Use **@hookform/resolvers** to integrate Zod with React Hook Form
- **Disable submit buttons** during form submission
- **Clear form state** after successful submission

```typescript
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { z } from 'zod';
import { Box, Button, Input, VStack, Text } from '@chakra-ui/react';

const schema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1, 'Title is required'),
  description: z.string().optional(),
});

type FormData = z.infer<typeof schema>;

function MyForm() {
  const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors, isSubmitting } } = useForm<FormData>({
    resolver: zodResolver(schema),
  });

  const onSubmit = async (data: FormData) => {
    // Handle submission
  };

  return (
    <Box as="form" onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)}>
      <VStack spacing={4}>
        <Input {...register('title')} placeholder="Title" />
        {errors.title && <Text color="red.500">{errors.title.message}</Text>}
        <Button type="submit" isLoading={isSubmitting}>
          Save
        </Button>
      </VStack>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

### Navigation Patterns
- Use **React Router DOM 6.28.2** for all navigation
- Use **useRoutes** hook for route configuration
- **Implement breadcrumbs** with back navigation
- Use **programmatic navigation** with useNavigate hook

```typescript
import { useNavigate, useParams } from 'react-router-dom';
import { Button } from '@chakra-ui/react';

const navigate = useNavigate();
const { id } = useParams<{ id: string }>();

// Navigation examples
<Button onClick={() => navigate('/')}>
  ← Back to Dashboard
</Button>
```

### Accessibility
- Include **aria-label** attributes for interactive elements
- Use **semantic HTML** elements
- Ensure **keyboard navigation** support
- Provide **alternative text** for images
- Use **Chakra UI components** which have built-in accessibility

```typescript
import { Input, IconButton } from '@chakra-ui/react';
import { FiSearch } from 'react-icons/fi';

<Input 
  placeholder="Search by title" 
  aria-label="Search positions by title"
/>

<IconButton
  aria-label="Search"
  icon={<FiSearch />}
/>
```

## Testing Standards

### Unit and Integration Testing with Vitest
- **Test components** using React Testing Library
- Use **data-testid** attributes for reliable element selection
- **Organize tests by feature** (CandidateCard.test.tsx, etc.)
- **Mock API calls** using Vitest mocks or MSW (Mock Service Worker)

```typescript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';
import { CandidateCard } from './CandidateCard';

describe('CandidateCard', () => {
  it('should render candidate name', () => {
    render(<CandidateCard name="John Doe" score={85} step="Screening" />);
    expect(screen.getByText('John Doe')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### Component Testing with Storybook
- **Document components** using Storybook
- **Test component variations** with stories
- **Use Storybook addons** for accessibility testing (@storybook/addon-a11y)

```typescript
// CandidateCard.stories.tsx
import type { Meta, StoryObj } from '@storybook/react';
import { CandidateCard } from './CandidateCard';

const meta: Meta<typeof CandidateCard> = {
  component: CandidateCard,
};

export default meta;
type Story = StoryObj<typeof CandidateCard>;

export const Default: Story = {
  args: {
    name: 'John Doe',
    score: 85,
    step: 'Screening',
  },
};
```

### Test Organization
- **Group related tests** with describe blocks
- **Use descriptive test names** that explain the expected behavior
- **Test both success and error scenarios**
- **Include edge cases** and validation testing
- **Place test files** next to components (Component.test.tsx) or in __tests__ directories

## Configuration Standards

### TypeScript Configuration
- Enable **strict mode** for type checking
- Use **path mapping** with "@/*" for cleaner imports
- Configure **verbatimModuleSyntax** for proper type-only imports
- Use **project references** for better build performance

```json
{
    "compilerOptions": {
        "strict": true,
        "baseUrl": "./src",
        "paths": {
            "@/*": ["*"]
        },
        "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
        "target": "ES2022",
        "module": "ESNext",
        "jsx": "react-jsx"
    }
}
```

### ESLint Configuration
- Use **ESLint 9.x** with flat config format
- Include **React hooks rules** (eslint-plugin-react-hooks)
- Include **TanStack Query rules** (@tanstack/eslint-plugin-query)
- Include **Testing Library rules** (eslint-plugin-testing-library)
- **Automatic code formatting** and error detection
- **Consistent code style** across the project

### Environment Configuration
- Use **Vite environment variables** (VITE_* prefix)
- Access via `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`
- **Separate configurations** for development and production
- Create `.env.example` file for documentation

```typescript
// vite.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  // ... config
});

// Usage in code
const apiUrl = import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL;
```

## Performance Best Practices

### Component Optimization
- **Lazy load** components when appropriate
- **Memoize expensive calculations** with useMemo
- **Avoid unnecessary re-renders** with useCallback
- **Extract reusable logic** into custom hooks

### Bundle Optimization
- **Tree shaking** enabled through Vite
- **Code splitting** at route level (React.lazy, Suspense)
- **Optimize images** and static assets
- **Monitor bundle size** with Vite build analyzer
- **Vite HMR** for fast development experience

### API Efficiency
- **Implement proper error handling** for network requests
- **Cache API responses** where appropriate
- **Use loading states** to improve perceived performance
- **Batch API calls** when possible

## Development Workflow

- **Feature Branches**: Develop features in separate branches, adding descriptive suffix "-frontend" to allow working in parallel and avoid conflicts or collisions
- **Descriptive Commits**: Write descriptive commit messages in English
- **Code Review**: Code review before merging
- **Small Branches**: Keep branches small and focused

### Development Scripts
```bash
npm run dev        # Start Vite development server
npm run build      # Production build (TypeScript check + Vite build)
npm run preview    # Preview production build
npm test           # Run Vitest tests
npm run test:ui    # Run Vitest with UI
npm run lint       # Run ESLint
npm run storybook  # Start Storybook dev server
npm run storybook:build  # Build Storybook for production
```

### Code Quality
- **ESLint validation** before commits
- **TypeScript compilation** without errors
- **All tests passing** before deployment
- **Performance monitoring** with Web Vitals

## Migration Strategy

### TypeScript Migration
- **Gradual migration** from JavaScript to TypeScript
- **New components in TypeScript** by default
- **Maintain existing JavaScript** components until planned refactor
- **Add types incrementally** to existing code

### Component Modernization
- **Functional components** over class components
- **Hooks** instead of lifecycle methods
- **Chakra UI v3** components for consistency
- **TypeScript** for all new components
- **Responsive design** principles throughout
- **Feature-based organization** (features/ directory)

This document serves as the foundation for maintaining code quality and consistency across the LTI frontend application. All team members should follow these practices to ensure a maintainable and scalable codebase.
